{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An arbitrary circle can intersect the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f378c4afca0b93937ed0aa3420a6f6a351e1e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> in\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/76935addd2811e3c66810d61c8bc3e71d670b9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\text{at most }2\\text{ points} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }\\text{at most }4\\text{ points} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } \\text{at most }6\\text{ points} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\text{at most }8\\text{ points}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"714\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d689b49a7dbf43a7535da34b3f4a8d9706de3318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E) \\  }\\text{more than }16\\text{ points}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a circle whose center lies on the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis and which passes through the origin. As the radius of this circle becomes arbitrarily large, its curvature near the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis becomes almost flat, and so it can intersect the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f378c4afca0b93937ed0aa3420a6f6a351e1e49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" /> arbitrarily many times (since the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis itself intersects the curve infinitely many times). Hence, in particular, we can choose a radius sufficiently large that the circle intersects the curve at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6da4e5494a4c569b7ec75cdf32bca8cb170af22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E)} \\ \\text{more than }16 \\text{ points}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"191\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index